# probe_pair_bound_name_as_a_number.gy — a name the pair road bound is read as a number.
#
# The arithmetic a slot's answer takes travels to the binding as a (payload, tag) pair (ADR 0267), and
# this program asks every position that wants one static number to read it: an operand of a sum, a
# negation, an ordering, a condition's head, a `while` head, an `and`, `str`, an f-string field, and the
# target of an augmented assignment. Each of them refused one commit ago with the missing pair named
# (roadmap Gap R.143); every line now answers the same on CPython, `--interp` and `--aot`.
#
# A float is bound beside an int on purpose: the tag is what decides `17.5` from `17`, and a position
# that read the payload alone would print the box handle underneath it. What this program does *not*
# ask is a position that takes a whole value — a builtin's argument, a container's element, an `and`'s
# operand — which is the next door over (Gap R.146, programs/probe_pair_bound_name_takes_a_value).
xs = []
xs.append([7, 8])
n = xs[0][0] * 2
print(n + 1)
print(n - 1)
print(-n)
print(n > 13)
print(13 > n)
print(1 if n > 1 else 0)
if n:
    print("truthy")
i = 0
while n > 0 and i < 2:
    print(n)
    i = i + 1
    n = n - 1
print(str(n))
print(f"[{n}]")
q = xs[0][1] * 3
q += 1
print(q)
r = xs[0][0] * 2.5
print(str(r))
print(r > 17)
print(f"{r}")
